attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Karn, Silver Golem blocks or becomes blocked, it gets -4/+4 until end of turn.\\n{1}: Target noncreature artifact becomes an artifact creature with power and toughness each equal to its mana value until end of turn.', "Whenever Retromancer becomes the target of a spell or ability, Retromancer deals 3 damage to that spell or ability's controller.", 'Whenever Seasoned Marshal attacks, you may tap target creature.', 'Whenever Viashino Weaponsmith becomes blocked by a creature, Viashino Weaponsmith gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever a Forest is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional {G}.', "Whenever a creature dies, if another creature is on the battlefield, return the first card to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", "Whenever a creature dies, that creature's controller may draw a card.", 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, you gain life equal to its toughness.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield, its controller sacrifices a creature or land.', 'Whenever a green creature dies, its controller discards a card.', 'Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, you may search your library for a card with the same name as that creature, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "Whenever a player casts a green spell, put a +1/+1 counter on Titania's Chosen.", 'Whenever a player casts a spell, that player discards a card.', 'Whenever a player casts an enchantment spell, counter it.', 'Whenever a player taps an Island for mana, Scald deals 1 damage to that player.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a creature spell, if Opal Acrolith is an enchantment, Opal Acrolith becomes a 2/4 Soldier creature.\\n{0}: Opal Acrolith becomes an enchantment.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a white spell, that player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever an opponent plays a land, if Hidden Stag is an enchantment, Hidden Stag becomes a 3/2 Elk Beast creature.\\nWhenever you play a land, if Hidden Stag is a creature, Hidden Stag becomes an enchantment.', 'Whenever another card is put into a graveyard from anywhere, exile that card.', "Wirecat can't attack or block if an enchantment is on the battlefield.", 'Worn Powerstone enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}.', "X target blocked creatures assign their combat damage this turn as though they weren't blocked.", 'You gain 6 life.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'You may choose not to untap Endoskeleton during your untap step.\\n{2}, {T}: Target creature gets +0/+3 for as long as Endoskeleton remains tapped.', "You may choose not to untap Mana Leech during your untap step.\\n{T}: Tap target land. It doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as Mana Leech remains tapped.", 'You may play an additional land on each of your turns.', 'Your opponents play with their hands revealed.', '{0}: Hopping Automaton gets -1/-1 and gains flying until end of turn.', '{1}, Sacrifice a permanent: You gain 1 life.', '{1}, {T}: Untap target artifact.', '{1}{U}: Counter target red spell.', '{1}{W}, {T}: Target creature becomes an enchantment and loses all abilities until a player casts a creature spell.', '{1}{W}: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn by target attacking creature with flying.', "{2}, Sacrifice a permanent: Return target creature to its owner's hand.", "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Pit Trap: Destroy target attacking creature without flying. It can't be regenerated.", '{2}{B}, {T}: Exile up to three target cards from a single graveyard.', '{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Crystal Chimes: Return all enchantment cards from your graveyard to your hand.', '{3}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', '{3}: Each player mills two cards.', '{4}, Sacrifice Copper Gnomes: You may put an artifact card from your hand onto the battlefield.', '{5}, {T}: Shuffle your library, then reveal the top card. Until end of turn, for as long as that card remains on top of your library, play with the top card of your library revealed and you may play that card without paying its mana cost. (If it has X in its mana cost, X is 0.)', '{B}: Looming Shade gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{B}: Regenerate Unworthy Dead.', '{B}{B}, {T}: Destroy target green creature.', '{B}{B}, {T}: Destroy target white creature.', '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Elvish Lyrist: Destroy target enchantment.', '{G}: Target creature gains trample until end of turn.', "{R}: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, return Viashino Sandswimmer to its owner's hand. If you lose the flip, sacrifice Viashino Sandswimmer.", '{R}: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield. That creature gains haste. Sacrifice the creature at the beginning of the next end step.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{R}, {T}: Shivan Gorge deals 1 damage to each opponent.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Add {B}{B}.', '{T}: Add {G} for each Elf on the battlefield.', '{T}: Add {G} for each creature you control.', '{T}: Add {U} for each artifact you control.', '{T}: Add {W} for each enchantment you control.', '{T}: Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.', '{T}: Destroy target creature with power 4 or greater.', '{T}: Elite Archers deals 3 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', '{T}: Fire Ants deals 1 damage to each other creature without flying.', '{T}: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', "{T}: Return Wizard Mentor and target creature you control to their owner's hand.", '{T}: Untap two target lands.', '{T}: You gain 1 life.', '{U}: Untap Horseshoe Crab.', "{U}: Untap Morphling.\\n{U}: Morphling gains flying until end of turn.\\n{U}: Morphling gains shroud until end of turn. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\n{1}: Morphling gets +1/-1 until end of turn.\\n{1}: Morphling gets -1/+1 until end of turn.", '{W}: The next time a black source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{W}: The next time a blue source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{W}: The next time a green source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{W}: The next time a land source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{W}: The next time a red source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{W}: The next time a white source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{W}: The next time an artifact source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{X}, {T}: Search your library for a creature card with mana value X or less, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', '{X}, {T}: Tap X target lands.', '{X}: Chimeric Staff becomes an X/X Construct artifact creature until end of turn.']
flavor: ['". . . But I\'m not tired!"', '"A ruler wears a crown while the rest of us wear hats, but which would you rather have when it\'s raining?"\\n—Barrin, *Principia*', '"All bonds are parasitic. Only rulership is pure."\\n—Gix, Yawgmoth praetor', '"All we could lose, we did. All we could keep, we do. And both are shrouded by mists."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"As a great whale dies, it flips onto its back. And so an island is born."\\n—Mariners\' legend', '"Ash is our air, darkness our flesh."\\n—*Phyrexian Scriptures*', '"Belief is the strongest mortar."', '"Believe in the ideal, not the idol."\\n—Serra', '"Books can be replaced; a prize student cannot. Be patient."\\n—Urza, to Barrin', '"Braid her branches, life fulfilling Goddess loving, Goddess killing."\\n—Citanul chant', '"By this glyph I affirm your role."\\n—Urza, to Karn', '"Death—an outmoded concept. We sleep, and we change."\\n—Sitrik, birth priest', '"Do not presume to speak for yourself."\\n—Gix, to Xantcha', '"Father of Machines! Your filigree gaze carves us, and the scars dance upon our grateful flesh."\\n—*Phyrexian Scriptures*', '"Fight? I cannot. I do not care if I live or die, so long as I can rest."\\n—Urza, to Serra', '"From void evolved Phyrexia. Great Yawgmoth, Father of Machines, saw its perfection. Thus the Grand Evolution began."\\n—*Phyrexian Scriptures*', '"From womb of nothingness sprang this place of beauty, purity, and hope realized."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 3', '"Give thy ration to thy mount, if the road be long. So sayeth the bey."', '"Gix doesn\'t want a people to rule but puppets to entertain his madness."\\n—Xantcha, Phyrexian outcast', '"Great Yawgmoth moves across the seas of shard and bone and rust. We exalt him in life, in death, and in between."\\n—*Phyrexian Scriptures*', '"Grief is as useless as love."\\n—Gix, Yawgmoth praetor', '"Here sprouted the first seedling of Argoth. Here the last tree will fall."\\n—Gamelen, Citanul elder', '"Here\'s how ya win. Don\'t let the other guy hit back first."\\n—Jula, goblin raider', '"How could you not hear it approach? It\'s a hippo!"\\n—Argivian commander', '"I don\'t understand why he works so hard on a device to duplicate a sound so easily made with hand and armpit."\\n—Barrin, progress report', '"I preferred the harsh tutors—they made mischief all the more fun."\\n—Teferi, third-level student', '"If fear is the only tool you have left, then you\'ll never control me."\\n—Xantcha, to Gix', '"If one harm us, strike them in return. So sayeth the bey."', '"If you can\'t catch them, cut the trees down from beneath them. Force them to fight on our terms."\\n—Mishra', '"If you kids don\'t stop that racket, I\'m turning this expedition around *right now!*"', '"In the gathering there is strength for all who founder, renewal for all who languish, love for all who sing."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 642', '"It followed me home. Can I keep it?"', '"It is *not* sad," Radiant chided the lesser angel. "It is right. Every society must have its outcasts."', '"It is not your place to rule, Radiant. It may not even be mine."\\n—Serra', '"It moved this way, an\' that way, an\' then before I could stick it, it jumped over my head an\' was gone."\\n—Jula, goblin raider', '"It only short jump. You go first."\\n"AIIIEEEE!"\\n"Hmm . . . we go different way now."', '"It will be the goblin\'s first bath, and its last."\\n—Fire Eye, viashino bey', '"Knowledge is no more expensive than ignorance, and at least as satisfying."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"Let Phyrexia breed evil in the darkness; my holy light will reveal its taint."\\n—Serra', '"Let go your mind. Mine is fitter."\\n—Gix, Yawgmoth praetor', '"Let weak feed on weak, that we may divine the nature of strength."\\n—*Phyrexian Scriptures*', '"Life\'s balance is as a star: on one point is Law, and Law must be upheld. If the knots of order are loosened, chaos will spill through."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 167', '"Lifted beyond herself, for that battle Brindri was an angel of light and fury."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 524', '"My finest warrior was lost to the Phyrexians. I pray that Lady Selenia died honorably."\\n—Radiant, archangel', '"Nothin\' beat surprise—\'cept rock."', '"Opposite Law is Grace, and Grace must be preserved. If the strands of Grace are unraveled, its design will be lost, and the people with it."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 167', '"Phyrexia\'s purity permits no other."\\n—Xantcha, Phyrexian outcast', '"Planeswalking isn\'t about walking. It\'s about falling and screaming."\\n—Xantcha, Phyrexian outcast', '"Protect our mother in her womb."', '"Push one goblin into sight, an\' run a lot. That\'s tactics."\\n—Jula, goblin raider', '"Shiv hatched from a shell of stone around a yolk of flame."\\n—Viashino myth', '"Shiv may be surrounded by water, but the mountains go far deeper."\\n—Fire Eye, viashino bey', '"Take the sharp metal stick and make a lotta holes."\\n—Jula, goblin raider', '"Tawnos\'s blueprints were critical to the creation of my armor. As he once sealed himself in steel, I sealed myself in a walking crypt."\\n—Urza', '"Teferi is a problem student. Always late for class. No appreciation for constructive use of time."\\n—Barrin, progress report', '"That they are saved from death is immaterial. What is important is that they know the source of their benefaction."\\n—Radiant, archangel', '"The answer to life should never be death; it should always be more life, wrapped tight around us like precious silks."', '"The clouds came alive and dove to the earth! Hooves flashed among the dark army, who fled before the spectacle of fury."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 211', '"The humans are useful in their way, but they must be commanded as the builder commands the stone. Be soft with them, and they will become soft."\\n—Radiant, archangel', '"The land putrefied at its touch, turned into an oily bile in seconds."\\n—Radiant, archangel', '"The most disappointing thing about learning telepathy is finding out how boring people really are."\\n—Teferi, fourth-level student', '"The solution can hide for only so long."\\n—Urza', '"The soul? Here, we have no use for such frivolities."\\n—Sitrik, birth priest', '"Their fragile world. Their futile lives. They obstruct the Grand Evolution. In Yawgmoth\'s name, we shall excise them."\\n—Oath of the East', '"Their weak laws. Their flawed systems. They inhibit the Grand Evolution. In Yawgmoth\'s name, we shall erase them."\\n—Oath of the West', '"Then, just when the other guys were winnin\', the sky threw up."\\n—Jula, goblin raider', '"They are bred to suffer and born to die. Much like humans."\\n—Gix, Yawgmoth praetor', '"Time flows like a river. In Tolaria we practice the art of building dams."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"To fill your mind with knowledge, we must start by emptying it."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"We decide who is worthy of our works."\\n—Gix, Yawgmoth praetor', '"We drive the dragons from our home. Why should we fear you?"\\n—Fire Eye, viashino bey', '"We each have our own strengths, Radiant," Serra said with a sly smile. "If all of my people were like this one, who would carry your scrolls?"', '"We have more sprouts than they have hands."\\n—Gamelen, Citanul elder', '"We plant the seeds of doubt to harvest the crop of wisdom."', '"Wear the foe\'s form to best it in battle. So sayeth the bey."', '"What do a hero and an arrow have in common? In times of war are many more made."\\n—Elvish riddle', '"When I say it rained, it was not small drops, but a thick, greasy drool pouring from the heavens."\\n—Urza, journal', '"When the sword becomes a burden, let the warrior lay it aside that another with a truer heart might take it up."\\n—Radiant, archangel', '"Without order comes errors, and errors kill on Tolaria."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"Xantcha is recovering. The medicine is slow, but my magic would have killed her."\\n—Serra, to Urza', '"Yawgmoth spent eons wrapping Phyrexians in human skin. They are the sleeper agents, and they are everywhere."\\n—Xantcha, to Urza', '"You reek of corruption," spat the knight. "Why are you even here?"', '"Your enemies will pound upon the door of your defenses, but only you shall have the key, and it is the key of life."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 873', "A dragon's scale can be carved into a mighty shield, provided you can procure a dragontooth to cut it.", "A foul, metallic stench clogged Urza's senses. It was then he knew his brother was no more.", 'A fragile cocoon of dreaming will.', 'A hollow dog is never empty. It is filled with thirst for the hunt.', 'A landslide of goblins poured toward the defenders—tumbling, rolling, and bouncing their way down the steep hillside.', 'A religious order for religious order.', 'A snake in the grasp.', 'After a hundred failed experiments, Urza was stunned to find that common silver passed through the portal undamaged. He immediately designed a golem made of the metal.', "Afterward, Tolaria's winds were like the whispers of lost wizards, calling for life.", "Ages ago, a party of elves took cover to let one pass. They're still waiting.", "All bark, someone else's bite.", 'All the pain of the shattered forest contained in a single drop.', 'Although some of the students quickly grasped the concept, the others could summon only blackboards.', 'Although the elves of Argoth always considered them a nuisance, the pixies made fine allies during the war against the machines.', 'Arrows fletched with the feathers of angels seldom miss their mark.', 'As Serra was to learn, the peace and sanctity of her realm were as fragile as glass.', 'At the academy, "show and tell" too often becomes "run and hide."', 'Beauty is beyond law.', 'Before Urza and Mishra came to Argoth, the herders prevented their creatures from stampeding. During the war, they encouraged it.', 'Birds frozen in flight. Sea turned to glass. Tolaria hidden in a mirror.', 'Both forge and pyre.', 'Bring the spear of ancient briar;\\nBring the torch to light the pyre.\\nBring the one who trod our ground;\\nBring the spade to dig his mound.', 'Buyer beware.', 'Catastrophes happened so often at the mana rig that the viashino language had a special word to describe them.', 'Designed to carry equipment across rivers, the hopping automaton was soon pressed into service in the infantry.', 'Devoured by the mists, Tolaria was stuck in time, trapped between two eternal heartbeats.', 'Does the stone mimic life, or did it once live?', 'Each day at dusk the birds above the canopy grow silent.', "Entire trees were stripped of their bark and branches by the wurm's writhing path.", 'Everything will find its use in Phyrexia. Eventually.', 'Few swim in a place of such thirst.', "Fiko summoned only atogs for three straight sessions. The tutor couldn't decide whether to punish his failure or praise his consistency.", 'Fire in the blood, fire in the belly.', "From deep in the caves beneath the forest, the hierophants planned the druids' raids against the enemy.", 'Gix despised the sylvan morass. The gouge that the portal had torn in the forest was the only pleasing sight.', "Harbin's ornithopter had been trapped for two days within the currents of the storm. When the skies cleared, all he could see was a horizon of trees.", 'He was proud to wear the lizard skin around his waist, just for the fun of annoying the enemy.', 'Here, rain does not wash the land; it desiccates it.', 'Hunger is a kind of madness—and here, all madness flourishes.', 'If only every message were as perfect as its bearers.', "If you're smaller than the anaconda, it considers you food. If you're larger than the anaconda, it considers you a lot of food.", 'In Argoth, the shortest path between two points is the one the swine make.', "In pursuit of Urza, the Phyrexians sent countless foul legions into Serra's realm. Though beaten back, they left it tainted with uncleansable evil.", 'In the final days before the disaster, all the crabs on Tolaria migrated from inlets, streams, and ponds back to the sea. No one took note.', 'Instead of creating a tool that would be damaged by heat, the Thran built one that was charged by it.', 'It has no face of its own—it wears that of its latest victim.', 'It is not unusual for a single family of coral merfolk to spend centuries carefully guiding the growth of the reefs where they make their home.', 'It soon became obvious that some experiments were best overseen by fireproof teachers.', 'It wants only to dress you in silk.', 'It was the dragons who first learned to chase their prey into the vapors before igniting them.', "It was the explorers' only tether to reality.", "It's all fun and games until someone loses an eye.", "It's not known whether the Thran built the device to forge their wonders or to defend them.", 'Its purr is the sound of iron filings sliding down satin.', 'Its spines are prized as writing quills by the priests of Gix.', 'Its windpipe is only the first to amplify its maddening laughter.', 'Late at night, ululations echo from deep under Shiv, as the wurms sing of times older than humanity.', 'Life is eternal. A lifetime is ephemeral.', 'Like a sleeping dragon, Shiv stirs and groans at times.', 'Living metal encasing dying flesh.', 'Many cultures have legends of a lush, hidden paradise. The elves of Argoth had no need of such stories.', 'Mother, sleep / Dream our lives Our roots your soul / Our leaves your bed.', 'On its way to the cave, the armadillo brushed by a sapling. It awoke to find a full-grown tree blocking its path.', 'Once heard, the battle song of an angel becomes part of the listener forever.', "Once you've seen one, you'll understand why spells won't go near them.", "One pounce, she's hungry—you die quickly. Two, she's teaching her cubs—you're in for a long day.", 'Peace to all. Peace be all.\\n—Great Hall floor inscription', "Phyrexia had tried to take Urza's soul. He was relieved that Shiv tried to claim only his soles.", 'Phyrexia wastes nothing. Its food chain is a spiraling cycle.', 'Radiant\'s eyes flashed. "Go, then," the angel spat at Serra, "and leave this world to those who truly care."', "Rainclouds don't last long in Shiv, but that doesn't stop the lightning.", "Red sky at night, dragon's delight.", 'Serra told them to guard Urza as he healed. Five years they stood.', 'Sharpen your ears\\n—Elvish expression meaning "grow wiser"', 'Shivan inhabitants are hardened to fire, so their predators have developed alternative weaponry.', 'Some roads are paved with bad intentions.', 'Sometimes quantity, in the absence of quality, is good enough.', 'Spells will shun you, as will everyone else.', "Start with eleven gnomes and a room of parts, and come morning you'll have ten and a monster the likes of which you've never seen.", 'That the Tolarian mists parted for the drakes was warning enough to stay away.', 'The academy worked with time—until time ran out.', "The academy's libraries were protected by fire-prevention spells. Even after the disaster, the books were intact—though forever sealed in time.", 'The best cure for a big ego is a little failure.', 'The druids found a haven in the cool limestone tunnels beneath Argoth. The invaders found only tigers.', 'The elves of Argoth were trained to ride these creatures, even when their mounts traveled upside-down.', 'The first Yawgmoth priest to harness their power was rewarded with several unique mutilations.', 'The first explorers found Argoth a storehouse of natural wealth—towering forests grown over rich veins of ore.', 'The flow of time was disrupted; like a flooding river it rose from its banks. Tolaria was drowned in an instant that stretched toward infinity.', 'The forest grew back so quickly that lumbering machines were suspended in the treetops.', 'The forest rose to the battle, not to save the people but to save itself.', 'The forest was too lush for the brothers to despoil—almost.', 'The giant was felt a few seconds before he was seen.', 'The gorilla beat its chest and threw great handfuls of leaves into the air. It howled challenge and showed its teeth. The mechanical soldier, not understanding, simply killed it.', "The helix was the finest example of Mishra's campaign strategy: if he couldn't have Argoth, no one could.", "The imps' warbling cries echo through Phyrexia's towers like those of mourning doves in a cathedral.", 'The key did not work on a single lock, yet it opened many doors.', "The mage felt as though he'd been in the stasis suit for days. Upon his return, he found it was months.", 'The mages of Tolaria found strange ways to spend their free time. Occasionally they had contests to see whose kite was eaten last.', 'The massive Argivian attack on their rooted kindred was a declaration of war to the treefolk.', 'The most effective way to destroy a spell is to ensure it was never cast in the first place.', 'The only alert the invaders had was the rustling of leaves on a day without wind.', 'The power of faith is quiet. It is the leaf unmoved by the hurricane.', 'The priest cast Xantcha to the ground. "It is defective. We must scrap it."', "The pungent smell of roasting flesh made both mages realize they'd rather break for dinner than fight.", 'The shade tracks victims by reverberations of the pipes, as a spider senses prey tangled in its trembling web.', 'The strength of law is unwavering. It is an iron bar in a world of water.', 'The true names of birds are songs woven into their souls.', 'The very young and the very old know best the song the angels sing.', 'The viashino believe that the oldest mountains hate everyone equally.', 'The viashino had learned how to operate the rig through trial and error—mostly error.', "The viashino knew of the cracked pipes but deliberately left them unmended to bolster the rig's defenses.", 'The year that the brothers landed on Argoth, the trees produced five times as many seeds as normal.', 'There are only two rules of tactics: never be without a plan, and never rely on it.', 'There are places so horrible that even the dead hide their faces.', "There's always room for one more.", "They are Phyrexia's couriers; the messages they carry are inscribed on their slick hides.", 'They certainly are.', 'They say dromosaurs are frightened of dogs, even little ones. There are no dogs in Shiv. Not even little ones.', 'Though the reaver is horrifyingly effective, its dorsal vents spit a highly corrosive cloud of filth.', 'Titania rewards all those who honor the forest by making them a living part of it.', 'To hone swords and dull minds.\\n—Whetstone inscription', 'Treacherous and unpredictable currents around Tolaria earned the nickname "serpent wakes."', 'Urza dared to attack Phyrexia. Slowly, it retaliated.', 'Urza saw the wall and realized that even if he tore every Phyrexian to pieces, they would still resist him.', 'Urza thought it a crusade. Xantcha knew it was a robbery.', 'Urza tried to rule the air, but Gaea taught him that she controlled all the elements.', 'Visitors to Shiv fear the dragons, the goblins, or the viashino. Natives fear the ants.', "We live on the serpent's back.\\n—Viashino saying", 'When Urza asked the viashino what it did, they answered: "It hums."', "When the Brotherhood of Gix dug out the cave of Koilos they found their master's severed hand. They enshrined it, hoping that one day it would point the way to Phyrexia.", 'When the giant returned for the night, he found a dead merfolk on his pillow. Although he praised the little guma, he inwardly wondered where she had hid the head.', "When the winds rock the trees, listen for voices in the creaking of the trunks. If you hear your name, you are one of the Goddess's chosen.", "When wind marries sky, even the bride's veil sings her praises.", "When you've got nothing, you might as well trade it for something else.", 'Within the rig settlement, those who have mastered the making of weapons earn highest honor.', "Yawgmoth brushed Urza's mind, and Urza's world convulsed.", 'Yotian soldiers were designed to fight, not watch their feet.', 'You are not prey until a predator knows of your existence.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Andrew Goldhawk', 'Andrew Robinson', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Berry', 'Bob Eggleton', 'Brian Despain', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chippy', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Ciruelo', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Daren Bader', 'Dermot Power', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Donato Giancola', 'Greg Simanson', 'Greg Staples', 'Hannibal King', 'Heather Hudson', 'Henry G. Higginbotham', 'Jeff Laubenstein', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jerry Tiritilli', 'Jim Nelson', 'John Avon', 'John Matson', 'Jon J Muth', 'Kev Walker', 'Lawrence Snelly', 'Mark A. Nelson', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Raabe', 'Paolo Parente', 'Pete Venters', 'Randy Elliott', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Rob Alexander', 'Robh Ruppel', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott Kirschner', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Stephen Daniele', 'Steve Firchow', 'Steve White', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Tom Fleming', 'Val Mayerik', 'Vincent Evans', 'rk post']
