rulings: ['[{\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': "Because the “search” requires you to find a card with certain characteristics, you don\'t have to find the card if you don\'t want to."}, {\'date\': \'2019-06-14\', \'text\': "If an effect refers to a “[subtype] spell” or “[subtype] card,” it refers only to a spell or card that has that subtype. For example, Goblin War Party is a card that references and creates Goblins, but it isn\'t a Goblin card."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': "If no card of the chosen type is found before your library empties, you don\'t get a card, but you do get to order all the cards in your library any way you choose."}, {\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': \'If you use this on a multi-card draw, each replaced draw is handled separately. In other words, you reveal and then put on the bottom of the library for the first card, then do the same for the second, and so on. In a multi-card draw you do not have to choose how many of those draws will be replaced before you do any drawing or use of this card.\'}, {\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': \'This replacement effect replaces the draw, so nothing that triggers on a draw will trigger.\'}, {\'date\': \'2007-07-15\', \'text\': "If your library is empty, Abundance can prevent you from losing the game for being unable to draw a card. If an effect or turn-based action would cause you to draw a card, you can replace that draw with Abundance\'s replacement effect. (It doesn\'t matter that you\'d be unable to actually draw a card.) Since Abundance\'s effect has you put a card into your hand instead of drawing a card, you\'ll never be forced to draw a card with an empty library."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': "It only returns to owner\'s hand if it is still on the battlefield at end of combat."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': "You can pay 0 life if you want, but it\'s not useful most of the time."}]', "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'A source of damage is a permanent, a spell on the stack (including one that creates a permanent), or any object referred to by an object on the stack. A source doesn’t need to be capable of dealing damage to be a legal choice.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Can be used even when there is no damage to prevent. It prevents the next damage (if any) from the source this turn.'}, {'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'Cycling is an activated ability. Effects that interact with activated abilities (such as Stifle or Rings of Brighthearth) will interact with cycling. Effects that interact with spells (such as Remove Soul or Faerie Tauntings) will not.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'A source of damage is a permanent, a spell on the stack (including one that creates a permanent), or any object referred to by an object on the stack. A source doesn’t need to be capable of dealing damage to be a legal choice.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Can be used even when there is no damage to prevent. It prevents the next damage (if any) from the source this turn.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Adding a counter is optional. If you forget to add one during your upkeep, you cannot back up and add one later.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If a non-creature with fungus counters on it leaves the battlefield, there is no effect.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If more than one Sporogenesis is on the battlefield and a creature with fungus counters on it leaves the battlefield, each Sporogenesis will put a Saproling onto the battlefield for each counter. In other words if there are N copies of Sporogenesis and the creature had M fungus counters, you get N * M Saprolings.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If one Sporogenesis leaves the battlefield, all fungus counters are removed even if other Sporogenesis cards are on the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Adding a counter is optional. If you forget to add one during your upkeep, you cannot back up and add one later.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If a player does not have enough permanents, they sacrifice all the ones they have.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Adding a counter is optional. If you forget to add one during your upkeep, you cannot back up and add one later.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can activate the ability (choosing no targets) even if there are no verse counters on it. It doesn’t do anything useful if you do this.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You count the number of counters, then divide up the prevention during the announcement of the ability. Each targeted creature receives the appropriate amount of damage prevention when the ability resolves.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Adding a counter is optional. If you forget to add one during your upkeep, you cannot back up and add one later.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'All damage being dealt to you at one time gets redirected to one Pariah. If you take 3 damage at once, all 3 damage goes to one Pariah. If you take damage from multiple creatures in combat, all the combat damage goes to one Pariah.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can attach this to an opponent’s creature, and all damage done to you is instead done to their creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Angelic Chorus does not trigger when creatures phase in or change controllers.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This does not trigger on a permanent being turned into a creature. That is just a permanent changing type, not something entering the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Because the “search” requires you to find a card with certain characteristics, you don’t have to find the card if you don’t want to.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If a copy card goes to the graveyard under this effect, you get to look for another copy of the card it was copying. This is because a copy card actually takes on the name and initial characteristics of what it copies.'}, {'date': '2010-03-01', 'text': 'If a card which is a creature only due to an effect goes to the graveyard, you can search for another copy of that card even though the card in your library won’t be a creature card.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Because the “search” requires you to find a card with certain characteristics, you don’t have to find the card if you don’t want to.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Buyback causes a spell to go to your hand instead of your graveyard, so using Buyback will avoid triggering this card to be sacrificed.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Discarding does trigger this.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Can be used if a player has less than 2 cards in their library. It will remove 0 or 1 cards if that is all that is available.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It is not a draw effect so it will not cause a player with less than 2 cards in their library to lose.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Since you are putting more than one card in the graveyard at one time, each affected player can choose the order the 2 cards go in.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Can target an already tapped creature if you want.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Can target itself.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Changes into a creature even if the spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It triggers when the spell is cast, which means it becomes a creature before that spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into an enchantment, it is no longer a creature.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'A “creature spell” is any spell with the type Creature, even if it has other types such as Artifact or Enchantment. Older cards of type Summon are also Creature spells.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Counts cards during resolution.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Damage assignment choices from Trample and other things which allow alternative damage assignments for attacking creatures are all made by you.'}, {'date': '2010-03-01', 'text': 'With the exception of ignoring the damage assignment order, you follow all the normal rules for damage assignment.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Does not increase the mana cost of the spell. It just requires a separate expenditure in order for it to succeed.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When this spell resolves, you either pay X mana or let your lands become tapped. The lands that become tapped are not “tapped for mana”. If you choose to pay, you may pay the X mana using whatever mana abilities you want to use.'}, {'date': '2010-03-01', 'text': 'Only lands that actually have mana abilities will get tapped. This includes basic lands and lands with mana abilities printed on them, as well as lands which have been granted a mana ability by some effect.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Does not stop enchantments from being put onto the battlefield by a spell or ability.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This effect triggers when the spell is announced and prior to allowing responses to it.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Does not target the creature it damages.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Does not trigger on lands put onto the battlefield by a spell or ability.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Each activation is considered a new damage effect. An activation can only be 1 point of damage.'}, {'date': '2011-06-01', 'text': 'It will stay on the battlefield if there is a creature that is put into the graveyard during the end step. This is because this ability will not trigger at all if there is at least one creature on the battlefield as the end step begins.'}, {'date': '2011-06-01', 'text': 'Note that “until end of turn” effects wear off after “at the beginning of the end step” triggered abilities, so an artifact that animates until end of turn can keep this on the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'External effects that generate more mana still generate their additional mana as directed without being affected by this card. Effects which generate more mana based on what type of mana the land produces will be affected in color but not in amount.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The second ability of this card is a replacement effect, not a triggered ability.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You choose whether to sacrifice a creature or not on resolution. If not, then you sacrifice Contamination. You can choose to not sacrifice even if you no longer control Contamination on resolution.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If a spell is countered, it still counts as the one spell cast.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When Arcane Laboratory enters the battlefield, it will look back over the turn to see if any spell was cast before it entered the battlefield. It will notice itself being cast.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it leaves the battlefield, the effect ends and all players are able to cast spells unrestricted again.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If a spell or ability damages multiple things, divide up the damage before applying this effect, and prevent the 1 damage to you only.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It is a prevention effect applied when damage would be dealt.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If an effect asks you to discard a card, you can’t “discard” something that is in your graveyard. Those cards are not in your hand. Thus, Cycling abilities of cards in the graveyard can’t be activated.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If you cast a Buyback spell, then there will be two effects trying to replace where the card goes. You get to choose if the Buyback returns the card to your hand or the card gets exiled.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If you play a card using Yawgmoth’s Will and something triggers only when “cast from your hand”, that something will not trigger. Such things trigger based on where the card came from.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It will exile itself since it goes to the graveyard after its effect starts.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The second ability creates a replacement effect. It applies to both costs and effects.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'To “play a card” is to either cast a spell or to put a land onto the battlefield using the main phase special action.'}, {'date': '2006-10-15', 'text': 'You cannot Suspend a card from your graveyard, only your hand.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If any of the targets are not there on resolution, the others are still affected.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You pick the 0, 1, 2, or 3 target cards on announcement.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If it attacks more than once per turn, it gets the bonus each time.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If it manages to block or become blocked more than once in a turn, it can get the bonus twice.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Switching blockers will not re-trigger this since it only triggers on becoming blocked and switching does not unblock and reblock it.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If more than one of these is on the battlefield, the controller sacrifices a creature for each one of these.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the controller has no other lands or creatures on the battlefield, they must sacrifice the creature that just entered the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the creature changes controllers before this ability resolves, its new controller has to sacrifice something.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Tainted Aether’s controller is the one that controls its triggered ability, but the controller of the creature that entered the battlefield chooses what creature they sacrifice during resolution.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If multiple creatures are coming back, they come back one at a time, not all at once. This is because Lifeline triggered once for each creature and set up a separate “at end of turn” effect for each.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It fails to bring the creature back if the creature is not still in the graveyard at the end of turn.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It works for all players and has errata to remove the “your graveyard” text.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The creature comes back even if Lifeline leaves the battlefield after triggering, but before it resolves.'}, {'date': '2010-03-01', 'text': 'If more than one creature is on the battlefield and all the creatures on the battlefield go to the graveyard at once, then none of them are returned at end of turn. This is because Lifeline’s ability has an intervening-if clause, which means that there must be at least one creature on the battlefield at the time the ability resolves.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If spell is used to destroy Planar Void, it goes to the graveyard, then the spell goes to the graveyard. The spell is not exiled, as Planar Void was not on the battlefield when it was put into the graveyard.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The card does go to the graveyard before it is exiled, so other triggered abilities will trigger on the card going to the graveyard.'}, {'date': '2008-05-01', 'text': 'It will not trigger on itself going to the graveyard, or on any other cards going to the graveyard at the same time. This means that neither itself nor other cards put into the graveyard at the same time as it will get exiled.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the cards being put onto the battlefield also require choices, those choices are made after all players choose their card. The active player makes choices for their card (if any), then the other players (if any) in turn order.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Players choose cards during resolution, not announcement.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The current player chooses first, then each other player chooses in turn order. A player does not have to reveal the chosen card, so long as it is clear *which* card was chosen. After all choices are made, the cards are put onto the battlefield simultaneously.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the chosen creature to exchange is not on the battlefield at resolution, then sacrifice this card.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This ability is targeted, so Protection can prevent targeting if it exists when the ability would be put on the stack. Once the ability is on the stack, adding Protection will not counter the ability but the exchange will not take place since the target is illegal and you sacrifice this card on resolution.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the creature is on the battlefield and is returned to its owner’s hand or is exiled, this card loses track of the creature and has no further effects in the future.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the creature leaves the battlefield before this resolves, it still damages the player.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the damaged creature takes both lethal damage and is destroyed by this effect, you have to regenerate the creature twice to keep it alive.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the opponent has no cards in hand, this has no effect.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the player has no cards in hand, this has no effect.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the red spell damages more than one target, add 1 to each target.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The ability is a replacement effect which is applied when damage would become dealt.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the spell is no longer on the stack when the triggered ability resolves, the converted mana cost of the spell is still remembered.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It changes into a creature even if the spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It triggers when the spell is cast, which means it becomes a creature before that spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the spell was colorless (an artifact), this card does not get any form of Protection.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It changes into a creature even if the spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It triggers when the spell is cast, which means it becomes a creature before that spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'A “creature spell” is any spell with the type Creature, even if it has other types such as Artifact or Enchantment. Older cards of type Summon are also Creature spells.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If there is an artifact or enchantment on the battlefield (even your own) when this card enters the battlefield, you must return one to owner’s hand. If not, then simply ignore the “enters the battlefield” ability.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can cast this card if there are no artifacts or enchantments on the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If you have less than 4 cards, discard all you have.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If you have zero or negative life, half your life is zero, so it costs nothing to use the ability.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If your library is shuffled or that card otherwise leaves the top of your library, the effect ends.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The card is removed from the top of the library when you play it, just like a card is removed from your hand when you play it.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'While you do not have to pay the mana cost, you do have to pay any other costs described in the text that are paid when playing the card. If the cost in the card text is optional, such as with Buyback, you can optionally pay that cost.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It can end up holding more than one creature tapped.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can choose the same creature more than once (for no additional effect).'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It can trigger even if a player’s hand is empty momentarily during the middle of the resolution of a spell or ability.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It changes into a creature even if the spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It triggers when the spell is cast, which means it becomes a creature before that spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You choose whether to pay or not on resolution. If not, then you sacrifice the creature. You can choose to not pay if you do not control the creature on resolution.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It changes into a creature even if the spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It triggers when the spell is cast, which means it becomes a creature before that spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'A “creature spell” is any spell with the type Creature, even if it has other types such as Artifact or Enchantment. Older cards of type Summon are also Creature spells.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': \'It changes into a creature even if the spell is countered.\'}, {\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': \'It triggers when the spell is cast, which means it becomes a creature before that spell resolves.\'}, {\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': \'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.\'}, {\'date\': \'2008-08-01\', \'text\': "A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn\'t matter how long the permanent has been a creature."}]', "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It changes into a creature even if the spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It triggers when the spell is cast, which means it becomes a creature before that spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It changes into a creature even if the spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It counts how many cards you discard. Since this card will not be in your hand at that time, this card is not counted.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It looks back over the entire turn even if this card was not on the battlefield at the time.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'It reduces your life total to 1, not the damage to 1.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Worship does not prevent damage. It causes some damage to be unable to lower your life total. So any damage rendered useless by Worship was still dealt and is counted by effects that track the amount of damage done to a player. In addition, Worship does not prevent loss of life, so loss of life bypasses Worship.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Only affects lands on the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Only grants the ability to lands you control when this ability resolves.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The granted ability can be used while the land is tapped.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Players can get fewer than 3 cards if they want.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Players take 0 or 2 damage. Disorder does not do 2 damage per creature to the player.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Players with less than 2 cards discard all they have.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Since it is an Elf, it counts itself.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The ability can target an already untapped land.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The ability must target two different lands. It can’t be activated if there is just one land to target.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The ability does not trigger unless the player has more lands at the beginning of upkeep. This is checked again on resolution, and if the player does not still have more lands, no token is generated.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The ability has no effect if the player has no lands.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': \'The ability is never a mana ability.\'}, {\'date\': \'2011-01-25\', \'text\': "You get the mana whether you want it or not. If you don\'t spend it, it will disappear at the end of the current step (or phase)."}]', "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The ability is not a mana ability.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can target a different opponent each turn.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The blocking ability triggers only once no matter how many blockers are declared.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The bonus is continuously calculated.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The color is chosen on resolution.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The creature stops being a creature (or any other permanent type) and is just an enchantment with no abilities.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'A “creature spell” is any spell with the type Creature, even if it has other types such as Artifact or Enchantment. Older cards of type Summon are also Creature spells.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The creatures and lands are only prevented from untapping during the targeted player’s next untap step. They can still can untap during other player’s untap steps.'}, {'date': '2009-10-01', 'text': 'No creatures or lands controlled by the player will untap during their next untap step. This includes those which entered the battlefield after Exhaustion resolved.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The damage has no color. It is not red.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The number of cards in hand is counted on resolution of the ability.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The power of the creature is checked on activation and on resolution. If the targeted creature’s power is not 4 or greater on resolution, the ability doesn’t resolve.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': \'The swamps are counted on resolution.\'}, {\'date\': \'2010-08-15\', \'text\': "The amount of damage dealt to a creature is not bounded by its toughness, and the amount of damage dealt to a player is not bounded by that player\'s life total. For example, if Corrupt deals 6 damage to a 2/2 creature, you\'ll gain 6 life."}, {\'date\': \'2010-08-15\', \'text\': \'The life you gain is equal to the damage dealt by Corrupt, not necessarily to the number of Swamps you control (if some or all of the damage is prevented, for example).\'}, {\'date\': \'2013-07-01\', \'text\': \'Corrupt counts any land you control with the subtype Swamp, not just ones named Swamp.\'}]', "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The tokens are named “Goblin” and are of creature type “Goblin”.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The toughness is continuously calculated.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The triggered ability triggers when the creature spell is cast, and it is put on the stack before any responses can be cast or activated. This ability will resolve before that creature enters the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'A “creature spell” is any spell with the type Creature, even if it has other types such as Artifact or Enchantment. Older cards of type Summon are also Creature spells.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'They enter the battlefield tapped. They do not enter the battlefield and then tap afterwards.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This affects all creatures, not just your own.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This card is a bit weird. When it enters the battlefield under your control, you give control of it to an opponent. After that it damages them each turn because the “you” on the card means its controller.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This counts the lands on resolution.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This is a triggered mana ability. It does not go on the stack.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This is not modal. You do not have to choose the target type. The target has to either be a land or non-black creature when announced and on resolution.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Triggers at the end of every player’s turn.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'This card now uses the Reach keyword ability to enable the blocking of flying creatures. This works because a creature with flying can only be blocked by creatures with flying or reach.'}, {'date': '2008-05-01', 'text': 'The ability only triggers if the creature spell has flying, regardless of whether an effect would cause the creature to have flying once it entered the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'X can be zero if you want.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You look in your library but you do not have to choose a creature even if you have one that meets the criteria.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can sacrifice zero permanents if you want to.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can target already tapped lands.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You choose land or creatures when the spell resolves.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You choose the artifact card on resolution.'}, {'date': '2007-05-01', 'text': 'Putting the card onto the battlefield is optional. When the ability resolves, you can choose not to.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You choose whether to pay or not on resolution. If not, then you sacrifice Child of Gaea. You can choose to not pay even if you no longer control Child of Gaea on resolution.'}, {'date': '2009-10-01', 'text': 'If you do choose not to pay, but no longer control Child of Gaea, you cannot sacrifice. It will remain on the battlefield under its current controller’s control.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You choose whether to pay or not on resolution. If not, then you sacrifice Drifting Djinn. You can choose to not pay if you no longer control this card on resolution.'}, {'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'Cycling is an activated ability. Effects that interact with activated abilities (such as Stifle or Rings of Brighthearth) will interact with cycling. Effects that interact with spells (such as Remove Soul or Faerie Tauntings) will not.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You choose whether to pay or not on resolution. If not, then you sacrifice the creature. You can choose to not pay if you no longer control the creature on resolution.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You have to even match the color requirements of the mana cost.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You choose whether to sacrifice an enchantment or not on resolution. If not, then you sacrifice this card. You can choose to not sacrifice an enchantment if you no longer control this card on resolution.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You must target two different lands. You can’t choose to target just one.'}]", "[{'date': '2005-08-01', 'text': 'If you change this card’s target, you can change which Aura is targeted, but you can’t choose where that Aura will be moved.'}, {'date': '2005-08-01', 'text': 'Only targets the Aura and not either of the things the Aura may be on.'}]", "[{'date': '2005-08-01', 'text': 'Imaginary Pet’s ability triggers only if you have cards in your hand as your upkeep begins, and the ability checks again as it resolves. If your hand is empty at both those times, Imaginary Pet stays on the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2007-02-01', 'text': 'When Argothian Wurm enters the battlefield, first the active player gets the option to sacrifice a land. If they decline, the next player in turn order gets the option. If a player elects to sacrifice a land, Argothian Wurm is put on top of its owner’s library, but then all remaining players still get the option. If all players decline, then nothing happens and Argothian Wurm stays on the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2007-05-01', 'text': 'Creatures with the Reach ability (such as Giant Spider) don’t actually have Flying, so they can’t block this.'}]", "[{'date': '2007-07-15', 'text': 'If you sacrifice No Rest for the Wicked on the same turn you cast it, all creature cards that were put into your graveyard from the battlefield that turn will be returned to your hand, including any that were put into your graveyard before No Rest for the Wicked entered the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2007-07-15', 'text': 'It doesn’t matter who controlled the creature cards when they were on the battlefield. As long as they were put into your graveyard, you get to put them into your hand.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2007-07-15\', \'text\': \'You can\\\'t put an Aura card from your hand onto the battlefield this way if that Aura can\\\'t legally enchant Academy Researchers. For example, you can\\\'t put an Aura with "enchant land" or "enchant green creature" onto the battlefield attached to Academy Researchers (unless Academy Researchers somehow turned into a land or a green creature before the ability resolved).\'}]', "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Because the ability is targeted, it is not a mana ability. It can only be activated when you have priority, and goes on the stack like other non-mana abilities.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Creatures damage the defending player or planeswalker even if the blocking creatures are no longer there at that time.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If a creature is attacking a planeswalker, assigning its damage as though it weren’t blocked means the damage is assigned to the planeswalker, not to the defending player.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'This card now has Enchant Swamp, which works exactly like any other Enchant ability. This means it can only be cast targeting a Swamp, and it will be put into its owner’s graveyard if the permanent it’s attached to ever stops being a Swamp.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A Goblin permanent card is an artifact, creature, land, and/or enchantment card with the creature type “Goblin”. Usually such cards will be creatures in addition to any other types, but they may be tribal instead. For example, you could put Boggart Shenanigans onto the battlefield with this effect.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}, {'date': '2009-10-01', 'text': 'If Chimeric Staff is already an artifact creature when you activate its ability, Chimeric Staff stays an artifact creature but the ability resets its creature types. You always apply the effect from this card before counters or other effects that modify power and toughness. For example, if you pay {3} to make it a 3/3, then someone gives it -1/-1, it will be a 2/2. If you then activate the ability with {4}, you will apply the “4/4” effect before the -1/-1 effect, so the end result will be a 3/3. Damage that was dealt to the creature stays on it.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'Cycling is an activated ability. Effects that interact with activated abilities (such as Stifle or Rings of Brighthearth) will interact with cycling. Effects that interact with spells (such as Remove Soul or Faerie Tauntings) will not.'}, {'date': '2009-10-01', 'text': 'A token’s owner is the player who created it.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'Cycling is an activated ability. Effects that interact with activated abilities (such as Stifle or Rings of Brighthearth) will interact with cycling. Effects that interact with spells (such as Remove Soul or Faerie Tauntings) will not.'}]", "[{'date': '2010-08-15', 'text': 'Only Shiv’s Embrace’s controller (who is not necessarily the enchanted creature’s controller) can activate its activated ability.'}, {'date': '2010-08-15', 'text': 'When Shiv’s Embrace’s activated ability resolves, the creature Shiv’s Embrace is enchanting at that time will get +1/+0 (regardless of what creature Shiv’s Embrace was enchanting when the ability was activated). If Shiv’s Embrace has left the battlefield by then, the creature it was enchanting at the time it left the battlefield will get +1/+0.'}]", "[{'date': '2011-01-25', 'text': 'Any of this mana that isn’t spent during your upkeep step will be removed before your draw step begins. You cannot save it to be spent on the card you will draw this turn.'}]", "[{'date': '2011-01-25', 'text': 'You get the mana whether you want it or not. If you don’t spend it, it will disappear at the end of the current step (or phase).'}]", "[{'date': '2013-04-15', 'text': 'Affected creatures lose all other colors and are mono-black.'}]", "[{'date': '2014-09-20', 'text': 'If some of the creatures are illegal targets as Arc Lightning tries to resolve, the original division of damage still applies but no damage is dealt to the illegal targets. If all targets are illegal, Arc Lightning doesn’t resolve.'}, {'date': '2014-09-20', 'text': 'You choose how many targets Arc Lightning has and how the damage is divided as you cast the spell. Each target must receive at least 1 damage.'}]", "[{'date': '2016-06-08', 'text': 'Argothian Enchantress’s last ability will resolve before the spell that caused it to trigger.'}, {'date': '2016-06-08', 'text': 'Enchantments put onto the battlefield without being cast won’t cause Argothian Enchantress’s last ability to trigger.'}, {'date': '2016-06-08', 'text': 'If the enchantment spell is countered, Argothian Enchantress’s last ability still resolves and causes you to draw a card.'}]", "[{'date': '2016-06-08', 'text': 'Effects that modify a creature’s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Seal of Strength, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness.'}, {'date': '2016-06-08', 'text': 'Humble doesn’t counter abilities that have already triggered or been activated. In particular, casting this spell won’t stop a creature’s ability that says “At the beginning of your upkeep,” “When this creature enters the battlefield,” or similar from triggering.'}, {'date': '2016-06-08', 'text': 'Humble overwrites all previous effects that set the creature’s base power and toughness to specific values. Any power- or toughness-setting effects that start to apply after Humble resolves will overwrite this effect.'}, {'date': '2016-06-08', 'text': 'If the affected creature gains an ability after Humble resolves, it will keep that ability.'}]", "[{'date': '2016-06-08', 'text': 'You choose which lands to untap as the spell resolves. They aren’t targeted, and they don’t have to be lands that you control.'}]", "[{'date': '2016-06-08', 'text': 'You choose which lands to untap as the triggered ability resolves. They aren’t targeted, and they don’t have to be lands that you control.'}]", "[{'date': '2017-11-17', 'text': 'Fog Bank’s prevention effect isn’t considered while assigning combat damage from a creature with trample. For example, if it blocks a 5/5 creature with trample, that creature’s controller must assign 2 of that creature’s combat damage to Fog Bank and the remainder can be assigned to the defending player or planeswalker.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2018-03-16\', \'text\': "If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Path of Peace tries to resolve, the spell doesn\'t resolve. No player gains life."}, {\'date\': \'2018-03-16\', \'text\': "You are a creature\'s owner if the card representing it began the game in your deck, or if it\'s a token that entered the battlefield under your control. If Path of Peace targets a creature that you own but an opponent controls, you\'ll gain 4 life."}]', "[{'date': '2018-12-07', 'text': 'In a multiplayer game, if a player loses the game, triggered abilities that player controls are removed from the stack and no more from that player can be added. This means that if a creature an opponent controls dies while you control Fecundity, and you lose the game before Fecundity’s triggered ability resolves (perhaps because you lost the game at the same time that the creature died), that player won’t draw a card.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2020-06-23\', \'text\': "If the spell is an illegal target when Rewind tries to resolve, perhaps because it was countered by another spell or ability, Rewind won\'t resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won\'t untap any lands."}, {\'date\': \'2020-06-23\', \'text\': "Rewind targets only a spell. It doesn\'t target any lands. The lands are chosen as Rewind resolves."}, {\'date\': \'2020-06-23\', \'text\': "You can choose up to four lands, no matter who controls any of them. Those lands untap once. You can\'t choose one land and have it untap four times, for example."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-08-07\', \'text\': "If you don\'t have three cards in hand when instructed to discard three cards, you discard your hand."}, {\'date\': \'2020-08-07\', \'text\': "Use the sacrificed creature\'s power as it last existed on the battlefield to determine how many cards you draw."}, {\'date\': \'2020-08-07\', \'text\': "You draw and discard cards all while Greater Good\'s ability is resolving. Nothing can happen between the two, and no player may choose to take actions."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-08-07\', \'text\': "You sacrifice the creature only if you still control it at end of turn. If that creature has left the battlefield, even if it came back, you don\'t sacrifice it."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-11-10\', \'text\': "As Victimize resolves, you must sacrifice a creature if able. You can\'t change your mind and choose not to sacrifice anything."}, {\'date\': \'2020-11-10\', \'text\': "If one of the targeted creature cards is an illegal target (for instance, because it has left your graveyard before Victimize resolves), you\'ll still sacrifice a creature and put the other card onto the battlefield. If both are illegal targets, Victimize won\'t resolve. You won\'t sacrifice a creature."}, {\'date\': \'2020-11-10\', \'text\': "The creature you sacrifice isn\'t chosen until Victimize resolves. You can\'t return the creature you sacrifice because it will still be on the battlefield at the time targets are chosen."}, {\'date\': \'2020-11-10\', \'text\': "You must choose two targets. You can\'t cast Victimize targeting only one creature card."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2021-06-18\', \'text\': "Skirge Familiar\'s activated ability is a mana ability. It doesn\'t use the stack and can\'t be responded to."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2022-12-08\', \'text\': "Gaining control of a permanent doesn\'t cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it."}, {\'date\': \'2022-12-08\', \'text\': "Gaining control of an Aura or Equipment doesn\'t change what it\'s attached to."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2022-12-08\', \'text\': "You might end up discarding the card you searched for. It\'s a gamble!"}]', "[{'date': '2022-12-08', 'text': 'Count the number of creatures as Congregate resolves to determine how much life is gained.'}]", "[{'date': '2022-12-08', 'text': 'Exploration’s ability is cumulative with other effects that allow you to play additional lands, including ones created by other Explorations you control.'}]", "[{'date': '2022-12-08', 'text': 'Flesh Reaver’s ability triggers whenever it deals any damage to a creature or opponent, not only combat damage.'}]", "[{'date': '2022-12-08', 'text': 'If Serra Avatar is no longer in your graveyard when its triggered ability resolves, you still shuffle your library.'}, {'date': '2022-12-08', 'text': 'The ability that defines Serra Avatar’s power and toughness works in all zones, not only the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2022-12-08', 'text': 'The player makes all choices as the triggered ability resolves. They permanent they choose to return to its owner’s hand, if any, isn’t targeted by the ability.'}]", "[{'date': '2022-12-08', 'text': 'Wild Dogs’s first ability will check life totals as your upkeep begins, before any player has the opportunity to take any actions. If no one player has more life than all other players at that time (i.e., if two or more players are tied for the most life), the ability won’t trigger at all. If the ability does trigger, it will check again as it tries to resolve. If no player has more life than all others by that point, the ability won’t have any effect. The player who had the most life as the ability triggered doesn’t have to be the same player as the one who has the most life as the ability resolves.'}]", "[{'date': '2022-12-08', 'text': 'You decide on resolution if you are tapping or untapping, and which kind of permanent you are affecting.'}]"]
foreign_names: ["[{'name': 'Abflug', 'text': 'Die verzauberte Kreatur erhält Flugfähigkeit.\\nWenn der Abflug aus dem Spiel auf dem Friedhof landet, bringe den Abflug auf die Hand seines Besitzers zurück', 'type': 'Verzaubere Kreatur', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '81d071b8-142e-40eb-a8ac-27ecb53aef33'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Lanzamiento', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '5a44e8e7-5187-4b98-b6db-720678811474'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Elan', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'c47a1897-6c27-4b0d-a89f-1bc73225299f'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Lancio', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '04a7b1c4-79fd-46de-ac8c-a8e48f2b96dc'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': '離陸', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '4c360f10-2238-4668-bbc9-299e0f4d3634'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Lançar', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '792ac8c0-e152-4f7e-94cf-21d9aad811ff'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Abgenutzter Kraftstein', 'text': 'Der Abgenutzte Kraftstein kommt getappt ins Spiel.\\n{T}: Erhöhe Deinen Manavorrat um zwei farblose Mana. Benutze diese Fähigkeit wie eine Manaquelle.', 'type': 'Artefakt', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'e6f28a32-e877-4273-b8c5-9f4fb8ea7c37'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Piedra de poder desgastada', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'c6915c12-229d-48e1-9c36-2c8f4f63331a'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Lithoforce usée', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'eb282758-f72c-47bf-b557-538a749053c9'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Pietra del Potere Consunta', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '0611f791-b470-4e59-ba71-b42a1ed1666d'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': '摩滅したパワーストーン', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '92f09702-8589-4fe4-ba5a-2c1802220c0f'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Powerstone Gasta', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'bc7711e4-fabf-4167-90ac-ae5daafdfe4b'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Abscheuliches Grablied', 'text': 'Du kannst während Deiner Versorgungsphase eine Lyrikmarke auf das Abscheuliche Grablied legen.\\n{1}{B},opfere das Abscheuliche Grablied: Zerstöre bis zu X nicht-schwarze Kreaturen Deiner Wahl, wobei X gleich der Anzahl an Lyrikmarken auf dem Abscheulichen Grablied ist. Diese Kreaturen können in diesem Zug nicht regenerieren.', 'type': 'Verzauberung', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '1b7eba41-b60b-4498-a299-460fcc225249'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Réquiem abominable', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '29f1c7d3-5898-47e1-bb0c-600c5e0badda'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Infâme requiem', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '6d1923e2-73c1-4c1a-b3f6-54453d00c7a0'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Requiem Maligno', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '22bbd71c-9fe2-4aac-8689-59646e819d50'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': '不快な鎮魂歌', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '08251eaf-7cdd-46e9-a3d5-22a68445bb81'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Réquiem Vil', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'c94b9105-471c-4cc3-b12e-3cfd8bc1fc2c'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Akademie von Tolaria', 'text': '{T}: erhöhe Deinen Manavorrat um {U} für jedes Artefakt, das Du kontrollierst.', 'type': 'Legendäres Land', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'cc34149e-8010-41a3-8daa-14466703dcdc'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Academia tolariana', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '6c6694f5-2acf-41d0-a2cb-ad1fb3ede710'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Académie Tolarienne', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'da67150a-53fd-4c1e-a136-6c25de7c92bb'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Accademia di Tolaria', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '27dbf753-8ef6-48a6-a91f-f77028c08b68'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'トレイリアのアカデミー', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '7343d198-7e32-4a09-ba0f-78b1a8583d69'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Academia Tolariana', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '1853ccf5-35c0-429a-8283-c8082160530f'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Albinotroll', 'text': 'Echo\\n{1}{G}: Regeneration', 'type': 'Beschwörung eines Trolls', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '5207a3f8-9744-4590-9a03-7f41d25a41ab'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Troll albino', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '2f07dd99-cef8-4792-ba8c-edce6c66ae68'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Troll albinos', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '19dd0ae0-193d-4674-b26e-55f52cd31a64'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Troll Albino', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '8246af13-642e-487d-8e56-42bed229648b'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'アルビノ・トロール', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '3e6a55b8-e08f-48e0-a9c9-02a27ed14077'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Trol Albino', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '70b94935-77e2-4eb0-80e7-c4ba4d9b5a26'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Algenteppich', 'text': 'Sprich den Algenteppich nur auf einen Sumpf.\\nWenn das verzauberte Land getappt wird, zerstöre dieses Land.\\nWenn der Algenteppich aus dem Spiel auf dem Friedhof landet, bringe den Algenteppich auf die Hand seines Besitzers.', 'type': 'Verzaubere Land', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '117d5c0e-1d5a-4683-89a1-f22dd4876109'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Algas propagantes', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '08006b2a-9448-44f5-9477-6fe1e18008ec'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Algue envahissante', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '329c1e92-6e7c-4f36-8c69-fbebe90dc18b'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Alghe Prolifere', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '45c2cbe7-205f-4623-9979-681b1aff546f'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': '藻の蔓延', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '03980d7b-9d45-4880-abbb-32c0c50cb064'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Algas Disseminadas', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'b82975c9-ea15-44c7-b2a6-4f5fc869d095'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Anakonda', 'text': 'Sumpftarnung', 'type': 'Beschwörung einer Ophis', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '9eb02898-a0ad-4b2f-9c03-79e816a41e0d'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Anaconda', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '9010d2c7-8dbb-4336-9da5-f3de642af184'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Anaconda', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '68390ea6-c38d-4954-ab2b-a00dcffbdcd1'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Anaconda', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '0beecdef-1b9a-4af4-b3b6-25549a36b2d3'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'アナコンダ', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'a31987a7-7171-49c7-abb6-4b22f2ef981b'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Anaconda', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '8490bb36-cb3